# Frontend UI theme

When adding or editing UI in `frontend/`, reuse `@bainbridge/shared-ui` — do not invent one-off chrome.

## Source of truth

- Tokens: `frontend/packages/shared-ui/src/theme.js` + `global.css` (`--color-*`, `--font-*`)
- Import UI from `@bainbridge/shared-ui`

## Prefer these components

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Header filter / compact picker dropdown | `CardSelect` |
| Form field native select | `Select` |
| Text input / textarea / labeled field | `TextInput`, `Textarea`, `Field` |
| List filters | `FilterBar`, `FilterField`, `HeaderFilterControls` |
| Buttons / CTAs | `Button` / `GlobalButton` (variants already themed) |
| Back navigation | `Button` with label starting with `Back` (Update COA outline-sm + chevron), or `variant="back"` |
| Search in page header | `PageHeaderSearch` |
| Dates | `DmyDateInput`, `PeriodCardPicker` |
| Status | `StatusBadge` (+ resolve* helpers) |
| Confirm / alert | `useConfirm`, `useAlert` |
| Loading | `LoadingOverlay` |

## Do / don't

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — custom native select / local input chrome
<select className={styles.mySelect}>...</select>
<input className={styles.input} />

// ✅ GOOD — shared theme
<CardSelect options={opts} value={value} onChange={setValue} ariaLabel="…" />
<Select value={value} onChange={onChange}>{children}</Select>
<TextInput value={value} onChange={onChange} />
```

- Do not redeclare `.input`, `.select`, button/pill chrome in page CSS modules when a shared component exists.
- Page CSS modules: layout/spacing only; colors/fonts via CSS variables from the theme.
- Modals/popups: same rules as pages (filters → `CardSelect`, forms → FormControls).
- New reusable chrome belongs in `frontend/packages/shared-ui`, not copied into a page.
